The flag parsing logic contains a bug where providing a filter flag (like `--sensitivity`) as the last argument without a value will cause the script to crash. Use a robust method that accounts for different flag formats by checking if the positional argument list is empty before shifting.

```suggestion
		--sensitivity) [[ $# -eq 0 ]] && { print_error "search: --sensitivity requires an argument"; return 1; }; filter_sensitivity="$1"; shift ;;
		--case)        [[ $# -eq 0 ]] && { print_error "search: --case requires an argument"; return 1; };        filter_case="$1";        shift ;;
		--status)      [[ $# -eq 0 ]] && { print_error "search: --status requires an argument"; return 1; };      filter_status="$1";      shift ;;
		--repo-path)   [[ $# -eq 0 ]] && { print_error "search: --repo-path requires an argument"; return 1; };   repo_path="$1";          shift ;;
```

